---
import Photo from './Photo.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { trainings, quotes } from '../data/proof';
---

<section class="on-flesh section--quiet" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="quote">
      <Photo caption="photo: Marry, mid-laugh, unposed" alt="Photo to come: Marry laughing" tone="ink" class="photo--quote" />
      <div class="quote__text">
        <span class="label" data-type>the person in the room</span>
        <h2 id="proof-title" class="display-l" data-scrub-words>About 2,000 people. <em>Nobody performed.</em></h2>
        <div class="prose" data-stagger>
          <p>I've been in a lot of rooms. The therapy room, the sex-positive scene, temple spaces. And in my own temple spaces I saw it again and again and again: when people go through the heart first, something unleashes. An erotic current, authentic and a little unruly, that nobody has to force.</p>
          <p>Over the years, that became what I'm known for. (And loved for, if I'm allowed to say that.)</p>
          <p>I'm a trained sex therapist and relationship therapist, and I've worked with about 2,000 people. I bring a therapist's skill into the room, and I teach so you can take it home.</p>
        </div>
        {trainings.length > 0 && (
          <ul class="label proof__trainings" data-reveal>
            {trainings.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
          </ul>
        )}
        <a class="link-arrow" href={url('about')} data-reveal>Meet Marry</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {quotes.length > 0 && (
      <ul class="proof__quotes" data-stagger>
        {quotes.map((q) => (
          <li>
            <blockquote>
              <p class="display-s">{q.text}</p>
            </blockquote>
            {q.context && <span class="label">{q.context}</span>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )}
  </div>
</section>
